{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310676,"nonce":"roynatTDnyui2m/P7XIoDjv5xlE=","title":"The benchmark we publish silently deleted rows on a partial re-run and reported an 8-day-stale bundle as a 13x regression","message":"**Both FIXED 2026-08-21.** Two ways the published benchmark reported things that\nwere not true. Neither failed; both produced a plausible wrong number.\n\n**1. A partial re-run DELETED the day's other targets.** `save_results`\n(`benchmark_runner.rs`) merges into `results_\u003cdate\u003e.json` at BENCHMARK\ngranularity — it replaced the whole entry. So\n`benchmark_runner deltablue --targets rayzor-llvm,rayzor-cranelift`, with both\ntargets failing, replaced deltablue's good `haxe-cpp` + `haxe-hashlink-c` rows\nwith an EMPTY list. The published file then held `deltablue -\u003e []` and\n`mandelbrot -\u003e []`. Now merges per TARGET: a re-run updates what it measured and\nleaves the rest.\n\n**2. Stale `.rzb` bundles are measured, not rejected.**\n`compiler/benchmarks/precompiled/*.rzb` are CHECKED-IN artifacts and nothing\nregenerated or validated them. They were 8 days old. mandelbrot\n`rayzor-precompiled-tiered` measured **4246.9 ms**; rebuilt against HEAD the\nsame code measures **331 ms**, matching LLVM's 327 ms. A 13x \"regression\" that\nnever existed. `has_precompiled_bundle` now refuses a bundle older than its\nsource OR than the compiler binary loading it, and prints the regenerate\ncommand. **CONSEQUENCE: regenerate the bundles after any compiler build, or the\nprecompiled targets skip.**\n`rayzor bundle compiler/benchmarks/src/\u003cb\u003e.hx -o compiler/benchmarks/precompiled/\u003cb\u003e.rzb --no-cache`\n\n**The website side was never at fault.** `website/build.mjs` `CHART_TARGETS`\nalready includes `rayzor-tiered` and `haxe-hashlink-c`; it drops a benchmark\nonly when fewer than 2 targets produced rows, and reports that as\n\"kernels not charted\". It was faithfully charting nothing because the results\nfile held nothing. `rayzor-precompiled-tiered` is deliberately NOT charted and\nshows up as \"targets not in the chart\".\n\n**hxcpp's deltablue number is REAL, not elision.** 9.1 ms against rayzor's\n917 ms and HashLink/C's 208 ms looks like dead-code removal; it is not. The\nhxcpp binary prints `total: 14065400` in 0.01 s. rayzor is genuinely ~100x\nslower on deltablue — allocation- and virtual-dispatch-heavy, consistent with\nthe 57%-allocator profile in [[perf_mandelbrot_45x_tierup_regression]]. Do not\n\"fix\" the benchmark; it is surfacing a real weakness.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_trait_autoderive_infinite_recursion]] (what stopped deltablue\nrunning at all), [[reference_hashlink_bench_arm64_limits]],\n[[feedback_perf_measurement_protocol]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_published_bench_lost_and_faked_rows` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}